tes":["The supplied name exactly matches the normalized official Steam name for the supplied App ID."],"research":{"steam":{"status":"success","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T10:19:48.056Z","error":null}},"steamMetadata":{"appId":"2218460","links":{"store":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/2218460/","officialWebsite":"https://witte-studio.de/","support":"https://steamcommunity.com/app/2218460/discussions/"},"storageRequirements":{"kind":"required_free_space","windows":{"minimum":{"value":5,"unit":"GB","display":"5 GB","approximateBytes":5000000000,"evidenceText":"Storage: 5 GB"},"recommended":{"value":5,"unit":"GB","display":"5 GB","approximateBytes":5000000000,"evidenceText":"Storage: 5 GB"}},"macos":{"minimum":null,"recommended":null},"linux":{"minimum":null,"recommended":null},"note":"Steam publishes required free space, not the exact installed or download size."},"controllerSupport":{"level":"partial","xboxCompatible":null,"xboxEvidence":null,"note":"Generic Steam controller support does not prove Xbox controller compatibility."},"playerModes":{"singlePlayer":true,"multiplayer":true,"coop":false,"onlineCoop":false,"localCoop":false,"lanCoop":false,"sharedOrSplitScreen":false,"pvp":true,"maximumPlayers":null,"maximumPlayersNote":"The public Steam app-details response does not provide a reliable exact player limit.","evidence":["Single-player","Multi-player","PvP","Online PvP"]},"genres":["Action","Casual","Indie"],"categories":[{"id":2,"description":"Single-player"},{"id":1,"description":"Multi-player"},{"id":49,"description":"PvP"},{"id":36,"description":"Online PvP"},{"id":27,"description":"Cross-Platform Multiplayer"},{"id":22,"description":"Steam Achievements"},{"id":29,"description":"Steam Trading Cards"},{"id":67,"description":"Camera Comfort"},{"id":68,"description":"Custom Volume Controls"},{"id":78,"description":"Adjustable Difficulty"},{"id":74,"description":"Playable without Timed Input"},{"id":69,"description":"Stereo Sound"},{"id":18,"description":"Partial Controller Support"},{"id":23,"description":"Steam Cloud"},{"id":15,"description":"Stats"},{"id":25,"description":"Steam Leaderboards"},{"id":62,"description":"Family Sharing"}]}},"content":{"status":"success","steamAppId":"2218460","steamName":"Bunny Guys!","sourceUrl":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/2218460/","fetchedAt":"2026-10-16T08:30:10.085072+00:00","locales":{"en":{"status":"source","provider":"steam","shortDescription":"Climb, fall, curse… uh, respawn, pretend it was intentional. Bunny Guys is pure parkour chaos where one wins and everyone else fails spectacularly. Perfect for players who treat suffering, respawning, and “I can do better” as a hobby.","detailedDescription":"Milestone\n\nAbout the Game\n\nClimb, tumble, and rage — the ruthless obstacle race for bunnies with nerves of steel.\n\nPlay alone or online against up to 8 players: whoever reaches the top wins. Everyone else… falls down in spectacular fashion.\n\nMaster dangerous parkour routes, dodge nasty traps, and jump with the precision of a bunny on espresso. One wrong step, one jump too early and boom, back to the start.\n\nChallenge your friends, chase each other through chaotic levels, and fight for a spot on the global leaderboard. Only the fastest earn the title “Golden Bunny” complete with an epic fireworks show.\n\nFeatures\n\n• \nChallenging climbing and parkour levels with fair checkpoints\n\n• \nOnline multiplayer for up to 8 players\n\n• \nGlobal leaderboard with time comparison\n\n• \nTraps, checkpoints, and wonderfully frustrating “One more try!” moments included\n\n• \nAverage playtime: 60–120 minutes… or hours? (highly dependent on fall rate)\n\nHow far will YOU get — and how many times will you have to start all over again?\n\nDeveloped by a Solo Developer\n\nHi! I'm Norman, the developer behind Witte Studio. Bunny Guys! is my solo developer project. What started as a simple idea turned into a pretty chaotic obstacle course where probably more bunnies fall down than actually reach the finish line.\n\nThe game has already driven quite a few players crazy – so, as a little apology, I decided to give away over 4 million copies during a free promotion. What could possibly go wrong?\n\nHave fun climbing, falling, and trying again!","aboutGame":"Climb, tumble, and rage — the ruthless obstacle race for bunnies with nerves of steel.\n\nPlay alone or online against up to 8 players: whoever reaches the top wins. Everyone else… falls down in spectacular fashion.\n\nMaster dangerous parkour routes, dodge nasty traps, and jump with the precision of a bunny on espresso. One wrong step, one jump too early and boom, back to the start.\n\nChallenge your friends, chase each other through chaotic levels, and fight for a spot on the global leaderboard. Only the fastest earn the title “Golden Bunny” complete with an epic fireworks show.\n\nFeatures\n\n• \nChallenging climbing and parkour levels with fair checkpoints\n\n• \nOnline multiplayer for up to 8 players\n\n• \nGlobal leaderboard with time comparison\n\n• \nTraps, checkpoints, and wonderfully frustrating “One more try!” moments included\n\n• \nAverage playtime: 60–120 minutes… or hours? (highly dependent on fall rate)\n\nHow far will YOU get — and how many times will you have to start all over again?\n\nDeveloped by a Solo Developer\n\nHi! I'm Norman, the developer behind Witte Studio. Bunny Guys! is my solo developer project. What started as a simple idea turned into a pretty chaotic obstacle course where probably more bunnies fall down than actually reach the finish line.\n\nThe game has already driven quite a few players crazy – so, as a little apology, I decided to give away over 4 million copies during a free promotion. What could possibly go wrong?\n\nHave fun climbing, falling, and trying again!"},"vi":{"status":"pending_translation","provider":null,"shortDescription":null,"detailedDescription":null,"aboutGame":null}},"media":{"images":[{"role":"header","url":"https://shared.akamai.steamstat